1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Genealogical accounts which attempt to connect Empress Gregoria to the royal Sassanid dynasty of Persia are spurious and based on no factual evidence. These name her as daughter of the emperor Shah-Varez and his w
2 CONC ife Dukhtzanan, herself the daughter of Chrosroes III Parver. They also provide [https://www.geni.com/people/Gregoria/6000000000944034143 Gregoria] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Konstantinos-III-Eastern-Roman-Emperor/6000000000
2 CONC 700960297 Constantine III] with a fictitious daughter, Manyanh, supposedly the wife of her Sassanid cousin, King Yazdagird III of Persia (632 – 651)." ("A Bit of History")
2 CONT
2 CONT She is mentioned in several articles at Wikipedia, but without citations. She is also not mentioned by MedLands.
2 CONT
