1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to Procopius, coins of Bawi were minted during the reign of Kavadh I (r. 488-496, 499-531) due to the marriage of the latter with his sister, and, therefore, he became the uncle of the future king Khosrau
2 CONC  I (r. 531-579).
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently he was the father of a person known as Asparapet, whose original name was Shapur, who was the grandfather of Shah Khosrau II (r. 591-528), the son of Shapur's daughter and Hormizd IV (r. 579-590); beyond this relationsh
2 CONC ip, it is known that Shapur was the father of Vistahm and Vinduyih.
