1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Bavand_dynasty see also : page 200 of  The Cambridge History of Iran - volume 4 https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=hvx9jq_2L3EC&lpg=PP1&pg=PA198&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Bav a son of Shapur and grand-newphew of Khusro I fled from Ctesiphon and established an empire in Tabaristan and Kohistan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His successors established the Bavandi dynasty. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The descendants of Bav stretched their territory to include parts of Shemiran, Qazvin, and even Taleshan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 679, Bav was killed by Valash. But the Bavandi dynasty was reinstated eight years later by Suhrab a son of Bav who married into the house of Ziyar.
