1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farrukh_Hormizd '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Farrukh Hormizd''' or '''Farrokh Hormizd''' (Persian: فرخ‌هرمز), was a spahbed in northern Persia, he was a prince of Atropatene.[1] He later came in conflict with the Sassanid nobles, "dividing the resources of the country".[2
2 CONC ] He was later killed by Siyavakhsh in a palace plot on the orders of Azarmidokht after he proposed to her in an attempt to usurp the Sasanian throne. He had two children, Rostam Farrokhzād and Farrukhzad.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Contents=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1 Family and origins
2 CONT * 2 Early career
2 CONT * 3 Usurpation and death
